<title>GREECE: Greek broker rankings for January.</title>
<headline>Greek broker rankings for January.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>January trading volume at the Athens bourse reached 520.7 billion drachmas, below the 577.16 billion traded in December 1996, the Athens stock exchange members association (SMEHA) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The monthly market share rankings showed Sigma Securities regaining the lead from National Securities with 9.38 percent, followed by Alpha Credit Bank subsidiary Alpha Brokerage with 7.59 percent.</p>
<p>National Securities fell to third place with 6.51 percent.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-to-December 1996 trading volume reached 3.979 trillion drachmas. December was last year's best month.</p>
<p>SMEHA released the following data and market share rankings for December. The top 15 brokers shared 62.5 percent of the bourse's trading volume. The remainder went to the exchange's other 47 member brokers.</p>
<p>	BROKER    VOLUME JANUARY	   MARKET SHARE (pct)</p>
<p>		    (in drs billion)</p>
<p> 1. Sigma		49.59		     9.38</p>
<p> 2. Alpha		40.12		     7.59</p>
<p> 3. National	   34.42		     6.51</p>
<p> 4. Telesis	    30.45		     5.76</p>
<p> 5. Devletoglou	29.05		     5.50</p>
<p> 6. Omega		19.10		     3.61</p>
<p> 7. Nuntius	    17.24		     3.26</p>
<p> 8. Midland	    16.93		     3.20</p>
<p> 9. Aspis		15.73		     2.98</p>
<p>10. Ergo		 15.71		     2.97</p>
<p>11. Intersec	   14.17		     2.68</p>
<p>12. Kappa		12.73		     2.41</p>
<p>13. Commercial	 12.29		     2.33</p>
<p>14. Hellenic	   12.28		     2.32</p>
<p>15. ABN AMRO Axias   10.94		     2.07</p>
<p>    Total Volume    520.70</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
